WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.000
Flash-sale customers tap Pay. The checkout spinner keeps turning, even though the database is healthy.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Each traditional platform thread waits while the payment API responds. A limited thread pool fills up.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Virtual threads allow many blocking requests to wait without occupying an operating system thread.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:40.000
But virtual threads do not increase database connections, payment capacity, or CPU throughput.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:50.000
Use bounded downstream concurrency, timeouts, idempotency keys, and a durable order state machine.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Load test queue time, p ninety nine latency, connection pool waits, and payment-provider errors.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Fewer requests stuck waiting for threads, without promising impossible throughput or duplicate-free payments.
